# The first message attaches a terminal to the workspace, once.
#
# `command` is what runs in the PTY. `tmux new -A -s main` gives reattach,
# scrollback and survival across disconnects for free: the socket's death
# kills the tmux CLIENT, while the server and the `main` session keep
# running in the workspace, so the next connection resumes the same screen.
# (The workspace image must have tmux; the Sprites image does.)
#
# `cols`/`rows` are the browser's initial terminal size; the page resizes
# later with a {"type":"resize"} control frame. `max_duration` bounds the
# whole session — the lease expires, the process is killed and the socket is
# told, whatever the client is doing — capped by --workspace-attach-max-duration.
#
# On success the chassis binds the PTY and returns `_attach.attached = true`
# with the lease id and expiry; from here the socket is the terminal. A
# transport/provider failure merges as top-level `workspace.error` (with
# `_attach = {}`), which the responder below renders.
WHEN .msg.type == "attach"
  EXEC "workspace://tools/attach"
    WITH command = "tmux new -A -s main",
         cols = .msg.cols,
         rows = .msg.rows,
         max_duration = "8h",
         into = "_attach"
